  auth.091.001.02_ESMAUG_DATREC_1.0.0
  (DerivativesTradeReconciliationStatisticalReportV02):
  Document > DerivsTradRcncltnSttstclRpt > RcncltnSttstcs/Rpt
  (one per RefDt × reconciliation-category cohort). Schema-shaped, not
  a fully XSD-valid instance. See docs/auth-messages/emir-auth091.md.

  auth.091 has no explicit pairing/recon rate; OpenDQI accumulates each
  TxDtls/TtlNbOfTxs by the cohort's Pairg/Rcncltn and DERIVES one rate
  per counterparty LEI. outstanding_* has no source -> EMIR.RST.
  OUTSTANDING_UNPAIRED_HIGH is unreachable from real auth.091.

  LEI-A: PARD/RECO 40, PARD/NREC 30, UNPR/RECO 10, UNPR/NREC 20
         -> pairing 70/100 = 0.70 (< 0.85 -> PAIRING_RATE_LOW),
            recon  50/100 = 0.50 (< 0.70 -> RECON_RATE_LOW).
  LEI-B: PARD/RECO 100 -> pairing 1.00, recon 1.00 (clean).
  LEI-C: under a NoRptgRqrmnt cohort -> no Pairg/Rcncltn, rates None
         (proves NoRptgRqrmnt cohorts are excluded).

  Each TxDtls/RcncltnRpt is ALSO projected onto a per-transaction
  ReconciliationRecord (UTI from TxId/UnqIdr/UnqTxIdr; pairing/recon
  status inherited from the enclosing cohort Pairg/Rcncltn;
  mismatched_fields = MtchgCrit criterion names where Val1 != Val2).
  These feed the existing EMIR.REC.* checks via emir recon-stats:
    U-A-2 (PARD/NREC)  -> PAIRED/UNRECONCILED            -> UNRECONCILED_TRADE
    U-A-3 (UNPR/RECO)  -> UNPAIRED/RECONCILED            -> UNPAIRED_TRADE
    U-A-4 (UNPR/NREC)  -> UNPAIRED/UNRECONCILED + 2 mismatched criteria
                          (CtrctTp scalar, CtrctVal nested) -> UNPAIRED_TRADE
                          + UNRECONCILED_TRADE + FIELD_MISMATCH (x2)
    U-B-1 (PARD/RECO)  -> PAIRED/RECONCILED, MtchgCrit all equal -> clean
    U-A-1, U-C-1       -> clean / no status
-->
